{
  "date": "2025-12-31",
  "period_start": "2025-12-01",
  "period_end": "2025-12-31",
  "title": "Video found its place in the garden",
  "summary": "December expanded Pollinations into a more complete multimodal workshop while making its growing community garden easier to build in, browse, and keep running.\n\nVeo and Seedance brought video generation into the platform, with image-to-video restoration, last-frame interpolation, duration and aspect-ratio controls, and clearer API support. GPT Image 1.5, Flux, Z-Image, Seedream, and SPAN upscaling also widened the image toolkit.\n\nAPI keys gained scoped model permissions, lifecycle and last-used data, unified dashboard handling, and permission-aware model discovery. Usage endpoints, public model stats, Markdown API docs, shared OpenAPI schemas, real-time streaming, and the React audio hook made the infrastructure more practical to integrate.\n\nNew creative tools, chat apps, games, learning projects, bots, and automation experiments arrived throughout the month, including several large catalog batches. App submission workflows gained smarter review handling, richer generated contribution PRs, and a single source of truth for the directory.\n\nModel routing and tool support were refined across Gemini, Claude, GPT-5, DeepSeek, Perplexity, and audio, while request deduplication, health monitoring, database indexes, account syncing, and model-monitor improvements made the shared machinery more legible and dependable.",
  "pr_count": 372,
